    <!--
      QtLoader preloads each entry here as lib<name>.so, AND separately loads the
      main library as lib<android.app.lib_name>_<abi>.so (see QtLoader.java: it
      sets MAIN_LIBRARY_KEY from android.app.lib_name, then appends
      libPrefix + lib + ".so" for every bundled_libs entry). Naming this entry
      plainly "ruby" therefore forced the SAME 15 MB libruby.so to be shipped a
      second time as lib/arm64-v8a/libruby.so, because the main library is
      libruby_arm64-v8a.so. Naming it "ruby_<abi>" makes one file satisfy both
      loads, which is the whole reason the APK was 15 MB fatter than it needed
      to be. Keep these names in sync with android.app.lib_name in
      AndroidManifest.xml if either side changes.
    -->
